00:31:41.310 --> 00:31:44.430
Yeah. But otherwise, I didn't think they were like ever too difficult to find.

00:31:44.550 --> 00:31:46.250
It would just encourage you more to explore.

00:31:46.590 --> 00:32:09.370
And I think that while I didn't have trouble finding them because it's a relatively small map, I think that the level design, like the actual creation of landmarks and recognizable environment is not conducive to finding keys and then finding the door again.

00:32:09.370 --> 00:32:12.210
Because it just, it looks all too samey to me.

00:32:13.290 --> 00:32:19.710
Whereas like if this, if this map was any bigger, it would be a problem because I wouldn't even know where the key I just found opens.

00:32:20.570 --> 00:32:27.450
Yeah. And the maps actually, if you look at them online, like now there's people who can capture the entire map and lay it out for you.

00:32:27.590 --> 00:32:29.670
If you look at them online, they're really not that big.

00:32:29.870 --> 00:32:32.450
I think the problem that we've already echoed is that they're very vertical.

00:32:32.750 --> 00:32:34.170
So that's when things become a problem.

00:32:34.430 --> 00:32:41.630
But if you take your time and actually like look through every crevice as you're going through it, you really won't have a hard time finding anything in this game.

00:32:41.770 --> 00:32:44.850
It's not like any, that's what this game is missing as well.

00:32:44.850 --> 00:32:47.050
You know, and I'm sorry that I'm always bringing up criticisms.

00:32:47.110 --> 00:32:52.630
I do think this is an okay game, but it's also missing like a puzzle aspect to it.

00:32:52.750 --> 00:32:54.910
There's no like, oh, I see that.

00:32:55.050 --> 00:32:56.330
How do I get that?

00:32:56.590 --> 00:32:58.990
You know, there's nothing really like that in this game.

00:32:58.990 --> 00:33:03.090
You'll mostly just get things by exploring and noticing them.

00:33:03.210 --> 00:33:08.710
And then like, you know, like I would have wished that some things would be hidden behind the items in the level themselves.

00:33:09.330 --> 00:33:11.730
And that's not really the case for most things.

00:33:11.890 --> 00:33:15.430
Yes, there's a time where like you'll need to levitate or something like that.

00:33:15.550 --> 00:33:17.490
But it's it's that's not really puzzle solving.

00:33:17.590 --> 00:33:20.990
That's just more like a barrier thing that make sure you get that before you do this.

00:33:21.290 --> 00:33:32.870
Yeah, it seems like this game could have just existed as not collecting gems, but just get key open door and that the gems were just there to pad time.

00:33:32.870 --> 00:33:47.230
Um, because as as long as you had those barriers, if you were able to create a level that use those barriers a little bit more creatively than they were in this game, it would have been just fine.

00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:48.970
You know what I'm saying?

00:33:49.210 --> 00:33:59.950
Yeah, no, totally. And the gems are the only reason why you have to collect them is because there is another knight who's red who looks just like you that like wants a certain number of gems before you can get through.

