Like more bones or just bigger bones?

00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:26.990
No, bigger bones.

00:40:27.210 --> 00:40:29.890
He drinks milk throughout the boss fight.

00:40:30.010 --> 00:40:30.970
Yeah, right on screen.

00:40:31.830 --> 00:40:34.450
Yeah, the whole thing was actually an advertisement for that campaign.

00:40:34.650 --> 00:40:39.070
To your guys' point, at least the first three bosses, it's the same fight.

00:40:39.070 --> 00:40:49.730
Yes. But what I was getting at was at least leading up to the second boss, I was actually having some trouble on those bats that are on the ceiling because they come down and they follow you.

00:40:49.870 --> 00:40:52.030
And as you go, there's like 20 of them.

00:40:52.270 --> 00:40:54.610
So you have to take out one at a time as much as you can.

00:40:54.710 --> 00:40:56.370
The further you go, the more bats come at you.

00:40:57.230 --> 00:40:59.710
And the later bats take more hits.

00:40:59.850 --> 00:41:02.630
So by the end, you need to hit three bats and there's like 10 of them on the screen.

00:41:02.790 --> 00:41:03.670
They're just killing you.

00:41:03.670 --> 00:41:08.810
Is it possible, though, that you are just continuously walking to the right throughout this whole portion?

00:41:09.450 --> 00:41:10.450
I mean, you could.

00:41:10.730 --> 00:41:11.610
That's what you do at first.

00:41:11.750 --> 00:41:12.730
You're not saying like...

00:41:12.730 --> 00:41:15.750
I'm saying that I would just take care of them at a time.

00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:17.070
Yeah, that's what I did.

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:21.790
Okay. But even that was tough because if you step accidentally a little too far, one comes down.

00:41:21.910 --> 00:41:29.170
Right. And when they attack you, hitting them three times, there's no kickback on the enemy.

00:41:29.190 --> 00:41:30.770
So you hit it once and it's still going to hit you.

00:41:30.890 --> 00:41:34.310
Take down three of your limited, what, 10 health?

00:41:34.590 --> 00:41:35.710
So then you've got to hit it again.

00:41:35.810 --> 00:41:37.010
Hits you again. That's another six.

00:41:37.170 --> 00:41:38.870
So you've got to be very careful as you're doing it.

00:41:38.990 --> 00:41:41.690
And what's weird is, is like you stamp a bat, you think it's dead.

00:41:41.790 --> 00:41:45.330
Right. Right? Not the ones that live deeper in the cave.

00:41:45.530 --> 00:41:46.610
Those are...

00:41:46.610 --> 00:41:47.790
Yeah, I don't know.

00:41:48.010 --> 00:41:49.150
I'm thinking like...

00:41:49.150 --> 00:41:50.070
Knife-resistant bats.

00:41:50.170 --> 00:41:51.950
Right, exactly. Exactly. But we...

00:41:51.950 --> 00:41:54.670
So we've talked about some of the bosses, but we haven't really talked about the levels.

00:41:54.750 --> 00:41:58.230
And I think there's a great motif with the map of going through...

00:41:58.230 --> 00:42:00.630
First you go through the forest and there's two forest stages.

00:42:01.130 --> 00:42:02.610
Then you get to the ice cave.

00:42:02.770 --> 00:42:04.830
Icy boys. And am I crazy or is this slippery?

00:42:05.070 --> 00:42:05.890
It's a little slippery.

00:42:06.110 --> 00:42:07.050
I think it's real. I actually didn't notice.

00:42:07.370 --> 00:42:08.170
I did notice.

00:42:08.630 --> 00:42:14.410
It's more apparent when you're trying to jump onto a ledge that has a slope next to it.

00:42:14.490 --> 00:42:18.390
Maybe that's where I noticed that slipperiness that I was talking about before.

00:42:18.710 --> 00:42:20.190
I just thought that was the whole game.

00:42:20.190 --> 00:42:21.850
Also, I was just being quiet.

00:42:22.050 --> 00:42:25.230
I didn't notice any kind of slipperiness in the first level.

00:42:25.470 --> 00:42:29.590
Because I do... The part I'm talking about where I kept trying to jump and kept missing was in that level.

00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:30.810
I remember that jump.

00:42:30.890 --> 00:42:32.910
I didn't even connect it with the ice. It was...

00:42:32.910 --> 00:42:37.530
Yeah, it was all... There's a lot of them in that stage where it's just like, am I supposed to get back up there

00:42:37.530 --> 00:42:39.350
or am I permanently locked out of that area?

00:42:39.490 --> 00:42:43.550
There was one part in particular I kept getting really, really close to...

00:42:43.550 --> 00:42:45.290
I was trapped. I knew I had to go back.

00:42:45.550 --> 00:42:46.570
I kept getting really close.

00:42:46.650 --> 00:42:50.530
I was pretty close to resetting the game thinking I locked myself in an impossible place.

00:42:50.770 --> 00:42:51.610
And then I got it.

00:42:51.710 --> 00:42:52.790
And I was like, oh, it is possible.

00:42:52.790 --> 00:42:56.990
So after the ice cave, Sean, you're our billiards expert.

00:42:56.990 --> 00:42:58.410
You're our NASA guy.

00:42:59.010 --> 00:43:00.430
You're our Mr.

00:43:00.610 --> 00:43:01.430
Science. Okay.

00:43:01.810 --> 00:43:03.170
Billiards are part of science.

00:43:03.330 --> 00:43:04.490
Yes. You're Mr. Science.

00:43:04.650 --> 00:43:11.110
Geometry. Would a ice cave be geographically located right next to a lava cave?

00:43:11.270 --> 00:43:18.030
See, what it could be is there is a massive air conditioner between the two.

00:43:18.290 --> 00:43:23.990
And what an air conditioner does is it cycles temperature gradients.

00:43:24.730 --> 00:43:29.630
And it could make the ice cave more icy and the lava cave more lava-y.

00:43:29.770 --> 00:43:31.070
We got it. If it's big enough.

00:43:31.250 --> 00:43:32.510
Okay. Yeah. Got it.

00:43:32.590 --> 00:43:35.810
Yeah, that makes sense. Also, Malkill is like a wizard.

00:43:35.810 --> 00:43:39.150
I was just going to say, you're probably forgetting the second paragraph of the manual.

00:43:39.410 --> 00:43:40.990
He is wizard Malkill.

00:43:43.870 --> 00:43:45.150
That's written like Bible.

00:43:45.510 --> 00:43:50.870
You know? It was also so great that, in fact, even the renowned Merlin was his pupil.

00:43:51.190 --> 00:43:53.390
But alas. I'm just running out of the manual.

00:43:53.390 --> 00:44:00.370
No, I know. I think it's funny that the guy who wrote the manual is listening to this episode and he thought that we were done like 20 minutes ago.

00:44:00.370 --> 00:44:04.250
And then all of a sudden you start reading again and he's like sweating bullets.

00:44:04.510 --> 00:44:06.430
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, manual writer.

00:44:07.010 --> 00:44:08.590
I enjoy it. He's like, I have a real job now.

00:44:08.710 --> 00:44:10.130
I didn't say anything bad about it there.

00:44:10.210 --> 00:44:11.450
I just said he is wizard Malkill.

00:44:11.790 --> 00:44:13.150
He is wizard Malkill.

00:44:14.430 --> 00:44:15.610
I am legion.

00:44:16.350 --> 00:44:22.490
So there's the ice cave, the lava cave, and then what is only referred to as the purple cave.

00:44:24.350 --> 00:44:25.990
So I like how there's a motif.

00:44:26.350 --> 00:44:27.390
There's the elements, you know?

00:44:27.450 --> 00:44:32.130
Yeah, yeah. Earth in the first one, ice, fire, and purple.

00:44:32.330 --> 00:44:33.450
Purple is...

00:44:33.450 --> 00:44:47.170
And what's funny is, like, purple doesn't have anything going for it other than the fact that, like, as far as, like, a motif goes, other than the idea that the apparition, who is that, like, grim reaper, ghost, ghoul-style thing, wears a purple robe.

00:44:47.330 --> 00:44:49.170
So clearly he would live in the purple cave.

00:44:50.390 --> 00:44:55.190
Every boss always color codes their sections by where they are.

00:44:57.030 --> 00:44:59.290
Wow. So that's all that.

00:44:59.550 --> 00:45:00.870
You get through all of that.

00:45:01.010 --> 00:45:02.730
Is there anything that we would have liked to see?

00:45:02.930 --> 00:45:04.130
Other elements or other...

00:45:04.130 --> 00:45:07.230
Other colors. You know, there's...

00:45:07.230 --> 00:45:08.830
Green is used in the forest.

00:45:09.030 --> 00:45:10.430
Blue is used in the...

00:45:10.430 --> 00:45:11.830
So what would be a yellow stage?

00:45:12.110 --> 00:45:14.070
The sun. Or a desert.

00:45:14.350 --> 00:45:16.850
Or a field of dandelions.

00:45:17.150 --> 00:45:19.390
I would have actually appreciated a desert.

00:45:19.470 --> 00:45:20.370
Yeah, desert would have been cool.

00:45:20.510 --> 00:45:21.590
Forest, it should have been...

00:45:21.590 --> 00:45:22.570
An underground desert?

00:45:22.830 --> 00:45:24.650
No, you could come out from the caves.

00:45:24.650 --> 00:45:33.890
Oh, okay. Yeah, it should have been, like, forest, ice cave, desert, lava cave, and then, um, purple cave.

00:45:34.070 --> 00:45:40.750
Sure. Purple cave, which would obviously lead you right back to the same forest.

00:45:41.030 --> 00:45:47.370
This is the weird thing about the map, is that the map only lets you go under the trees.

00:45:47.370 --> 00:45:50.310
If you're looking, if you're thinking about the map, you're climbing in those trees, but

00:45:50.310 --> 00:45:51.430
you're actually going down.

00:45:51.650 --> 00:45:53.470
Through the roots. You're going as a...

00:45:53.470 --> 00:45:58.430
You're making a giant U to get to the other side of the castle, whereas the map clearly

00:45:58.430 --> 00:46:02.750
shows that if you just would have kept walking right, you would show up to the castle.

00:46:02.770 --> 00:46:04.710
Yeah, but then you gotta deal with that much more forest.

00:46:05.490 --> 00:46:06.910
I mean, maybe it's...

00:46:06.910 --> 00:46:09.250
Maybe there's, like, a big rock in the way.

00:46:09.570 --> 00:46:10.490
I'm thinking...

00:46:10.490 --> 00:46:12.350
Like a Snorlax. A big rock makes sense.

00:46:12.390 --> 00:46:14.790
But it got there after the map was made.

00:46:14.970 --> 00:46:16.550
Yeah. So, like, it's not on the map.

00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:21.230
I'm also just thinking that maybe that, like, you know, because the spire of the top of the

00:46:21.230 --> 00:46:25.350
castle is so tall that, like, he would have seen you coming, and you want the element

00:46:25.350 --> 00:46:30.470
of surprise. So you're gonna come from the area right next to him with all the bushy trees.

00:46:30.670 --> 00:46:33.110
Right. Okay. Yeah. It's like the Lord of the Rings Eagles argument.

00:46:34.510 --> 00:46:36.630
The classic Lord of the Rings Eagles argument.

00:46:36.630 --> 00:46:37.830
Everybody knows that argument.

00:46:39.010 --> 00:46:44.370
And so you get to the castle exterior, and this is actually really cool when you're climbing

00:46:44.370 --> 00:46:51.650
up the castle, and they have, like, you actually see these really nice, like, shadow elements

00:46:51.650 --> 00:46:56.690
of the other spire casting on there, and, like, the triangles are really smooth.

00:46:56.710 --> 00:46:57.610
And you see...

00:46:59.250 --> 00:47:04.290
And you see the, like, bricks moving in and out in 3D space that you jump on.

00:47:04.290 --> 00:47:07.150
Wow, I really missed the best part of this game.

00:47:07.310 --> 00:47:08.530
The smooth triangles.

00:47:08.770 --> 00:47:11.350
The smooth triangles will blow your mind.

00:47:11.610 --> 00:47:12.570
It's just shading.

00:47:12.570 --> 00:47:17.270
It's just a shading trick, but it's actually some of the best sprite work we've seen.

00:47:17.530 --> 00:47:18.730
Ever. On the NES.

00:47:18.970 --> 00:47:22.450
Oh, okay. Not ever. But definitely some of the best sprite work we've seen on the NES.

00:47:22.650 --> 00:47:26.150
People who've gotten to the castle exterior will know exactly what I'm talking about.

00:47:26.230 --> 00:47:28.310
Shout out. You know what it reminded me of?

00:47:28.410 --> 00:47:33.210
It's just because of my own personal experience and no other reason, is that the level of Crash

00:47:33.210 --> 00:47:37.210
Bandicoot slippery climb where you're climbing the castle is very, very similar.

00:47:37.470 --> 00:47:38.270
No one's played Crash Bandicoot.

00:47:38.270 --> 00:47:39.650
Nobody in this room but me has played.

00:47:39.830 --> 00:47:42.190
I just wanted to make Joe feel weird.

00:47:42.890 --> 00:47:44.110
Well, you succeeded.

00:47:44.870 --> 00:47:45.750
Okay. I can't even say.

00:47:45.750 --> 00:47:46.750
I just don't remember that level.

00:47:46.990 --> 00:47:47.890
Otherwise, I'd agree with you.

00:47:47.950 --> 00:47:49.270
I'm sure. It's a good level.

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:50.570
One of my favorites. It's okay.

00:47:51.150 --> 00:47:54.250
So you get to the interior of the castle.

00:47:54.270 --> 00:47:56.230
You fight the growing skeleton.

00:47:56.870 --> 00:48:01.450
Otherwise, mostly the game is still at the same difficulty as most of it, and there's no real

00:48:01.450 --> 00:48:04.750
punishment, so just continue on if you're willing to trick through it.

00:48:05.210 --> 00:48:07.990
And you'll get to your face off with Malkil.

00:48:08.810 --> 00:48:13.690
He is a wizard all decked out in pink, so he's not scary at all.

00:48:14.470 --> 00:48:17.770
In fact, now I'm starting to question, am I the bad guy?

00:48:19.590 --> 00:48:22.170
He kind of looks like Gandalf a little bit, right?

00:48:22.250 --> 00:48:23.410
With the staff and everything.

00:48:23.850 --> 00:48:24.790
I actually didn't get to him. And the long beard.

00:48:25.410 --> 00:48:26.470
Oh, okay. I'm sorry.

00:48:26.570 --> 00:48:28.130
I didn't get to him either. I'm going to reveal.

00:48:29.010 --> 00:48:31.510
I actually, it's not that we couldn't get to him.

00:48:31.570 --> 00:48:35.490
I want to make it clear. I didn't have the patience to continue to play this game forward.

00:48:35.730 --> 00:48:42.070
I know. I did actually still want to keep playing, but then I tried to leave my system on, and

00:48:42.070 --> 00:48:44.810
I shut it off, and I didn't really want to go back through the whole game.

00:48:44.930 --> 00:48:47.890
Right. And the same thing I was saying, if I was punished to go back through the whole game, I wouldn't

00:48:47.890 --> 00:48:48.810
want to do it. You wouldn't want to do it, right?

00:48:48.810 --> 00:48:54.090
And that was proof. Can I just say real quick that I think it's weird that, yeah, you've got to save the princess,

00:48:54.090 --> 00:48:58.910
but all of the other women that you find throughout this game are just sort of incidental.

00:48:59.110 --> 00:49:02.610
Yeah. You're like, yeah, well, since I'm here, I guess I'll untie you, but that's it.

00:49:02.770 --> 00:49:03.610
Like, you're on your own. Yeah.

00:49:03.650 --> 00:49:06.450
I was like, oh, I could take it or leave it.

00:49:06.630 --> 00:49:10.090
I think maybe they just wanted to show you that Malkiel is like, he's not playing around.

00:49:10.210 --> 00:49:11.170
He's done this before.

00:49:11.290 --> 00:49:12.390
He's captured other women.

00:49:12.470 --> 00:49:14.370
I didn't know that there were other people captured you.

00:49:14.390 --> 00:49:15.590
You're like, oh my God, you're captured too?

00:49:15.710 --> 00:49:17.230
They're like named characters now.

00:49:17.450 --> 00:49:25.730
Yeah, like Penelope. Yeah, maybe Penelope is the other knight's lady, you know, and you're finally rescuing them.

00:49:25.870 --> 00:49:26.750
Right. Okay.

00:49:27.230 --> 00:49:31.930
The one thing that I have to mention with the battle with Malkiel is that the room that you're in,

00:49:31.990 --> 00:49:41.550
you'll never know it by playing the game, but if you actually get the map data, it's like a very, very cartoon skull.

00:49:42.010 --> 00:49:51.130
Aw. Like, with the eyes and everything, and it's actually, like, kind of funny, and I think that's weird.

00:49:51.570 --> 00:50:00.930
But Malkiel works in a very weird way that he teleports throughout the room, but it's not like, actually, it's kind of like Ganondorf, I guess.

00:50:01.110 --> 00:50:06.430
But the idea is that, like, wherever Malkiel will teleport to will usually be, like, near you.

00:50:06.970 --> 00:50:12.450
And so, if you move around the room a lot, you're not helping your odds of finding him.

00:50:12.610 --> 00:50:16.210
So you actually want to, like, when he teleports, you actually want to do the opposite of looking for him,

00:50:16.230 --> 00:50:20.190
and you just want to kind of stay still until he reveals himself to you again.

00:50:20.350 --> 00:50:23.110
So it's like, attack, attack, attack, like, as fast as you can.

00:50:23.370 --> 00:50:31.750
Yeah. And I think some guide online said that you want the boots of force for this battle, and I'm not sure why.

00:50:31.750 --> 00:50:38.850
Like, it says, you, oh, it says he won't avoid any particular locations just because you're there.

00:50:39.070 --> 00:50:42.370
You can even use the boots of force to kick him when he arrives.

00:50:42.570 --> 00:50:44.490
Aw. I like the idea that, like.

00:50:44.590 --> 00:50:46.530
It's just like a, it's just like a personal thing.

00:50:46.810 --> 00:50:48.950
Yeah. You're just like, yeah, I'm going to kick this guy.

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:52.710
You just nudge him. And that's the game.

00:50:52.970 --> 00:51:00.350
That's it. You defeat Malkiel, the usual supply of things appear,

00:51:00.350 --> 00:51:06.010
and then what's different is that killing Malkiel doesn't provide you with a pile of treasure,

00:51:06.250 --> 00:51:11.550
but instead it gives you the blue key, which you can escape from the room in the lower right corner,

00:51:12.190 --> 00:51:13.930
which is what the blue key requires.

00:51:14.110 --> 00:51:18.650
And then once you do, you'll rescue the princess and earn a 100,000 point bonus,

00:51:18.650 --> 00:51:20.090
which is quite a hefty bonus.

00:51:20.210 --> 00:51:22.450
Wow. And then the game will end.

00:51:22.450 --> 00:51:25.090
Where can you spend the points? You can't spend the points anywhere.

00:51:25.270 --> 00:51:26.830
Oh, yeah. You register your initials.

00:51:26.830 --> 00:51:28.130
Yeah, that's true, too.

00:51:28.330 --> 00:51:31.630
And I don't know who, I guess, like, you know, the game is, like I said,

00:51:31.810 --> 00:51:33.850
if it's only 45 to 50 minutes, if you know what you're doing,

00:51:34.090 --> 00:51:36.490
I guess you could try to get a new high score each time.

00:51:37.870 --> 00:51:41.010
But I don't care about high scores that I never have, and I never will.

00:51:42.590 --> 00:51:46.090
So that's, wow, you guys have lost your energy all of a sudden.

00:51:46.510 --> 00:51:47.970
This is Wizards and Warriors.

00:51:48.090 --> 00:51:49.130
Wizards and Warriors.

00:51:50.150 --> 00:51:58.610
I will mention on the cutting room floor of this game is that there was a map special item

00:51:58.610 --> 00:52:00.270
fully programmed into the game.

00:52:00.750 --> 00:52:03.610
You can still find it if you use, like, Game Genie or whatever,

00:52:03.790 --> 00:52:06.390
but you can't get it through normal means in the game.

00:52:06.810 --> 00:52:08.710
What you would do is you would press select,

00:52:08.710 --> 00:52:14.350
and it would bring up the map screen at any time rather than just at the beginning of the level.

00:52:14.590 --> 00:52:17.630
The map would then track where you are in the level.

00:52:17.630 --> 00:52:23.830
Oh. It would have come in handy in the early part of the game when you're trying to, like, collect things,

00:52:23.850 --> 00:52:27.970
and then the person notes, especially in the purple caves.

00:52:28.130 --> 00:52:29.950
I don't remember why in the purple caves.

00:52:30.030 --> 00:52:34.570
I guess it was just, like, everything's purple, so it's harder to navigate where you are.

00:52:34.770 --> 00:52:35.750
So that would have been nice.

00:52:36.050 --> 00:52:39.990
Were there any other, like, power-ups that we didn't see that we would have liked to see

00:52:39.990 --> 00:52:41.330
or quality of life improvements?

00:52:41.910 --> 00:52:43.170
We talked about the biggest ones.

00:52:43.170 --> 00:52:50.050
Yeah, I mean, I just think that this game could have really done with some better attack animations.

00:52:50.310 --> 00:52:51.470
Yes. I just...

00:52:51.470 --> 00:52:52.290
A lunge.

00:52:52.490 --> 00:52:57.330
Any kind of feeling power aside from your really heavy boots.

00:52:58.130 --> 00:52:59.090
Agreed, agreed.

00:53:14.810 --> 00:53:17.610
As I mentioned that the music was done by David Weiss,

00:53:17.830 --> 00:53:21.910
I did check an interview that he did with OC Remix,

00:53:21.910 --> 00:53:27.730
which is a fantastic website that does, like, you know, basically user-created remixes of video games,

00:53:27.750 --> 00:53:29.790
and you can basically search for your favorite games,

00:53:29.850 --> 00:53:33.590
and the chances are someone has done a remix of a song for that game,

00:53:33.730 --> 00:53:35.090
like, even very obscure ones.

00:53:35.550 --> 00:53:40.190
So this was DJ Pretzel, and he wrote to David in the interview,

00:53:40.190 --> 00:53:45.490
You started writing the main Wizards and Warriors theme when you were still in school

00:53:45.490 --> 00:53:49.410
as a means of using arpeggios to suggest a chord progression.

00:53:49.750 --> 00:53:55.710
Relative to the elaborate soundtracks being composed for big-budget Hollywood-scale games these days,

00:53:55.970 --> 00:53:58.150
this theme is relatively simple,

00:53:58.310 --> 00:54:03.690
yet more gamers remember it and remixers arrange it than many modern scores.

00:54:04.090 --> 00:54:05.470
Is simple better?

00:54:06.030 --> 00:54:07.550
David responds.

00:54:08.010 --> 00:54:09.670
Simple is always better.

00:54:09.670 --> 00:54:11.250
For something to sound simple,

00:54:11.510 --> 00:54:14.730
there has usually been a whole development cycle behind it.

00:54:14.930 --> 00:54:18.230
When I hear a piece of music and think I could have done that,

00:54:18.410 --> 00:54:23.390
I now think there has probably been a very involved process to hone down the melody

00:54:23.390 --> 00:54:25.070
to get to the final result.

00:54:25.270 --> 00:54:27.110
In the early days of video game music,

00:54:27.230 --> 00:54:29.270
with the limited resources we had at our disposal,

00:54:29.670 --> 00:54:31.490
the melody was incredibly important.

00:54:31.730 --> 00:54:35.270
To some extent, this has been taken over by other musical elements.

00:54:35.770 --> 00:54:37.430
That, in an ideal world,

00:54:37.430 --> 00:54:41.670
we would have liked to have used way back when we only had three channels.

00:54:42.230 --> 00:54:46.290
Yeah. I mean, I don't remember the music from this game,

00:54:46.290 --> 00:54:49.070
so I can't really comment on the quality of it,

00:54:49.210 --> 00:54:57.350
but whenever I think about music composition for machines this powerful,

00:54:57.570 --> 00:55:02.910
whether it's like the C64 or the NES or even as far up as the Super NES,

00:55:04.150 --> 00:55:08.530
it's amazing what they could do with the limited resources that they had.

00:55:10.690 --> 00:55:12.470
But, yeah, I just don't remember the music.

00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:19.090
See, I made a crack earlier about dying on purpose to not have to hear the low on health music,

00:55:19.090 --> 00:55:22.030
but that wasn't so much about that being bad.

00:55:22.030 --> 00:55:23.450
It wasn't my favorite for sure,

00:55:23.450 --> 00:55:26.990
but it was that I really did like the regular music in the different caves.

00:55:27.290 --> 00:55:28.750
Oh, okay. I think even in the forest,

00:55:28.910 --> 00:55:30.410
the first track,

00:55:30.510 --> 00:55:32.650
it's a little short of a loop,

00:55:32.670 --> 00:55:33.850
so I think it got repetitive,

00:55:34.110 --> 00:55:36.150
but I liked the music overall.

00:55:37.110 --> 00:55:40.430
Yeah, and I think one thing that should be echoed is the,

00:55:41.270 --> 00:55:43.290
you know, and this doesn't just apply to music.

00:55:43.290 --> 00:55:44.470
I think this applies to everything.

00:55:44.710 --> 00:55:47.110
The whole, I could have done that thought.

00:55:47.290 --> 00:55:49.330
Oh, yeah. Usually, if you have that thought,

00:55:49.530 --> 00:55:50.790
it's like, chances are,

00:55:50.790 --> 00:55:52.050
if you think you could do it,

00:55:52.170 --> 00:55:54.890
it's a lot harder to be the first one to do it.

00:55:55.010 --> 00:55:56.330
You know, I always think about that with art,

00:55:56.330 --> 00:55:57.470
even, and a lot of people are like,

00:55:57.530 --> 00:55:58.870
oh, that's art. I could do that,

00:55:58.930 --> 00:56:00.190
but it's like, but you didn't,

00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:01.450
you did it. You didn't do it now.

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:03.530
That's always the end of the conversation.

00:56:03.830 --> 00:56:06.950
And I don't even see that as like a slap to the face of the people.

00:56:07.130 --> 00:56:08.370
I mean that more in like a,

00:56:08.530 --> 00:56:10.210
really think about like what that means,

00:56:10.350 --> 00:56:12.390
and how like some of the best works of,

00:56:12.690 --> 00:56:15.850
or most remembered works of art in history,

00:56:16.750 --> 00:56:20.690
usually have to do more with the idea of how they resonate with a larger group,

00:56:20.790 --> 00:56:22.730
of people. It doesn't mean that they're necessarily the best.

00:56:22.910 --> 00:56:24.010
They're just what,

00:56:24.010 --> 00:56:26.110
like what has become public consensus,

00:56:26.110 --> 00:56:28.170
because it's, it resonates with more people.

00:56:28.270 --> 00:56:31.450
And I think that's why David thinks simple is better,

00:56:31.490 --> 00:56:33.630
because you can communicate bigger,

00:56:33.970 --> 00:56:37.450
you can communicate with a bigger audience when your ideas stay simple,

00:56:37.670 --> 00:56:38.510
but remain effective.

00:56:38.850 --> 00:56:40.630
Yeah. But I think that even anything,

00:56:41.370 --> 00:56:43.170
just because it sounds simple,

00:56:43.310 --> 00:56:44.590
or it looks simple,

00:56:44.730 --> 00:56:45.670
doesn't mean that it is.

00:56:45.850 --> 00:56:47.450
Totally. Like any kind of,

00:56:48.070 --> 00:56:53.930
a one note leading into another may be super easy if you're just playing those two notes,

00:56:54.010 --> 00:56:55.130
but in the larger whole.

00:56:55.610 --> 00:56:57.610
Yeah, to make something simple sound good.

00:56:57.750 --> 00:56:58.970
Yeah. Probably takes a lot, who knows,

00:56:59.130 --> 00:57:00.470
but probably takes a lot more thought.

00:57:00.670 --> 00:57:04.210
Oh, it does. And creativity than something that's more complex.

00:57:04.550 --> 00:57:06.510
Exactly. All right.

